  "claim": "The British man created the TV series \"Hippies\" alongside the creator of Toast of London. This man was also the creator of the Ash Atalla-produced sitcom for UK Channel 4.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Graham Linehan. Sentence: He is most noted for the sitcoms \"Father Ted\", \"Black Books\" and \"The IT Crowd\".\nPage: The IT Crowd. Sentence: The IT Crowd is a British sitcom by Channel 4, written by Graham Linehan, produced by Ash Atalla and starring Chris O'Dowd, Richard Ayoade, Katherine Parkinson, and Matt Berry.\nPage: Hippies (TV series). Sentence: It was created by Arthur Mathews and Graham Linehan, the writing partnership most famous for \"Father Ted\", but the scripts were written by Mathews alone.\nPage: Toast of London. Sentence: Toast of London is a British comedy television series created by Arthur Mathews and Matt Berry and starring Berry as Steven Toast, an eccentric, middle-aged actor with a chequered past who spends more time dealing with his problems off stage than performing on it.",
