        "original_id": "f056b625-3643-5419-9690-ff43d2dda40f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Graham Linehan, Arthur Mathews, Ash Atalla, Chris O'Dowd, Richard Ayoade, Katherine Parkinson, Matt Berry, Steven Toast\n- Works: Father Ted, Black Books, The IT Crowd, Hippies, Toast of London\n- Organizations: Channel 4\n- Topics: British sitcoms, comedy television, writing partnerships\n\nFacts:\n- Graham Linehan is most noted for the sitcoms Father Ted, Black Books, and The IT Crowd.\n- The IT Crowd is a British sitcom by Channel 4 that was written by Graham Linehan and produced by Ash Atalla.\n- The IT Crowd stars Chris O'Dowd, Richard Ayoade, Katherine Parkinson, and Matt Berry.\n- Hippies was created by Arthur Mathews and Graham Linehan.\n- Hippies was written by Arthur Mathews alone, although Arthur Mathews and Graham Linehan were the writing partnership most famous for Father Ted.\n- Toast of London is a British comedy television series created by Arthur Mathews and Matt Berry.\n- Toast of London stars Matt Berry as Steven Toast, an eccentric middle-aged actor with a chequered past who spends more time dealing with off-stage problems than performing.",
